   "body": "> Add support for background colors to theme rules.\r\n> \r\n> Closes #3429.\r\n> \r\n> I did this before noticing #3429. Maybe helps someone wanting to patch their own version.\r\n> \r\n> ## Example\r\n> ```js\r\n> id = 'patch'\r\n> tokenizer = {\r\n>   root: [\r\n>     [/^---\\s.*/, \"bredfill\"],\r\n>     [/^\\+\\+\\+\\s.*/, \"bredfill\"],\r\n>     [/^\\@\\@\\s.*/, \"bredfill\"],\r\n>     [/^-.*/, \"minus\"],\r\n>     [/^\\+.*/, \"plus\"],\r\n>   ],\r\n> }\r\n> \r\n> Mon.languages.register({ id: id,\r\n>                          firstLine: '^diff --git.*',\r\n>                          'mime-type': ['text/x-diff', 'text/x-patch', 'application/x-patch'],\r\n>                          extensions: ['.patch', '.diff'] })\r\n> Mon.languages.setMonarchTokensProvider(id, { tokenizer: tokenizer })\r\n> \r\n> themeSolarized.rules.push({ \"foreground\": '073642',\r\n>                             \"background\": 'eee8d5',\r\n>                             \"token\": \"bredfill\" })\r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> ![example](https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/32057441/329075571-c8c460bb-238f-475c-ab70-4426071ab8c4.png?jwt=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..LNd7E2Y6QkoKZZNjW5Aw01-RImFLpGzk8ICqDNF0QD0)\r\n\r\nHave you considered vscodium upstream? thank you for this, bless you",
   "author_association": "NONE",
